meta {
  name: Set a credential
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

put {
  url: {{bffUrl}}/api/v1/resources/{{integrationId}}/credential
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "secret_base64": "Z2hwX2V4ZW1wbG8tZGUtdG9rZW4="
  }
}

docs {
  The secret comes in through a request SEPARATE from the creation: it keeps the
  value out of the most logged and most retried call of all.

  **The response carries the resource without the value.** `credential_ref` is an
  opaque label that says there IS a credential, never which one — and there is no
  route to read the secret, nor must there come to be one. Whoever needs it is the
  executor, straight from the vault (ADR-0001).

  In an organization account, prefer an ORGANIZATION credential: a personal token
  dies when the person leaves (ADR-0003).
}
